r", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Rice Cookout", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Cashing in Rice", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about an unspecified time in the past that is related to now or continues up to now.</p>When you use the Present Perfect tense, the time when the action happened is not important.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect Continuous tense, the time when the action happened is also not important.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about:<ul><li>experience up to the present</li><li>change that has happened over time</li><li>an event or action that happened in the past that is important now</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Continuous</span>:<ul><li>to emphasize that action has continued without stopping until now and may still be taking place</li><li>when you can see the result of an action that happened in the recent past</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I have made dinner.</span> (dinner is ready to eat)<br/><span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I have been making dinner.</span> (I am still working on it or I just finished right now)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>Rice <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has become</span> the staff of life for half the nations in the world. </p><p>For the past hundred years, half of the rice consumed in the U.S. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has grown</span> there.</p><p>In North America our tastes<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> have changed </span> in the past quarter century.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>People <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been growing</span> rice for food in Eastern Asia for thousands of years.</p><p>Farmers <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been cultivating </span>rice in the U.S. in Virginia for 400 years.</p><p>Dishes from Asia <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have been turning up </span> in ethnic restaurants and Fusion Cuisine. </p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">For</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">In</span> for Duration", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span>, you often use phrases or clauses for duration.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These phrases or clauses begin with <span class=\"italic\">for</span>, <span class=\"italic\">in</span> or <span class=\"italic\">since</span>. They answer the question \u201cHow long ... ?\u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">since</span> to begin a phrase or a clause (as a connector or as a preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">for</span> and <span class=\"italic\">in</span> to begin a phrase (as a preposition).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Preposition</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for (the total amount of time)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">for thousands of years<br/>for the past few months<br/>for 400 years</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since (from the point in time that it started)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">since then<br/>since January<br/>since 2010</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in (inside that period of time)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">in the past decade<br/>in the past hundred years</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Connector</span></div>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"since (from the point in time that it started)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Since people have been shifting toward healthier, lighter foods ...</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Since people have been shifting toward healthier, lighter foods, she tells me, the consumption of rice has risen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Since then this practice has spread to other states. In the past hundred years, half of the rice consumed in the US has grown there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Farmers have been cultivating rice in the US in Virginia for 400 years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This means Americans have burned more rice in the past decade than any other people in the whole world!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the staff of life", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a necessary food; a staple food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In China, rice is the staff of life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about rice.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to emerge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to come out, to appear", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: \u201cHave you eaten your rice today?\" has emerged as a greeting in China.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cultivate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to grow on a farm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Farmers have been cultivating rice in the US in Virginia for 400 years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ethnic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "from a specific place and group of people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This city has a wide variety of ethnic restaurants.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Fusion cuisine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cooking that combines food traditions from different cultures in contemporary restaurants", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This restaurant is famous for its Fusion cuisine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "myriad", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large number", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are a myriad of choices when it comes to rice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to appear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show up; to become noticeable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: New types of rice are appearing in supermarkets.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk with your partner about the types of food you have tried.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a report on how your eating habits have changed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify a type of food that has become popular in your country and why you have or have not tried it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your report to a partner and discuss it. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss food I have tried.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about food that has become popular.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss how my eating habits have changed.", "type": "text"}]}]}